-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package (grepped content/ and seed/).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons could not be opened from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Wikimedia Commons thumbnails built from file names confirmed by search (MD5 path). The editor should confirm each license on the file page. The image check falls back to 800px or the original file if a thumbnail size is missing.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261124-huang-reinstated-trump', 'nvidia-reinstates-jensen-huang-ceo-after-trump-intervention', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Nvidia reinstates Jensen Huang as CEO after Trump pushes for his return', 'The board voted unanimously on Monday, Nov. 23, to bring Huang back, less than two weeks after he stepped down. Reuters reported that the reversal followed the president''s intervention.', 'Nvidia''s board reinstated Jensen Huang as president, chief executive and board director on Monday, Nov. 23, effective immediately, the company said in a release filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission. The board''s vote was unanimous, according to the release.

Reuters reported that the reversal came after President Trump pressed the board to bring Huang back. Trump told CNBC that he believed his intervention was very important in getting Huang reinstated, Reuters said.

## How it unfolded

Huang stepped down as CEO on Thursday, Nov. 12, after reports of extramarital affairs, according to Reuters. One of the reported relationships involved a former Megaspeed executive whom U.S. officials suspect of spying for China. China has denied the allegations. Huang has acknowledged being unfaithful and has apologized, Reuters reported.

Less than a week before the reversal, board chair Harvey Jones said the company would not rehire Huang, Reuters reported. Chief financial officer Colette Kress served as interim CEO and remains CFO, the company said.

## What the board said

In its release, Nvidia said it had received input from senior levels of the U.S. government and was confident that the reinstatement poses no national security risk. The company said Huang had been the target of a foreign intelligence effort. It said a committee of independent directors is investigating with independent counsel and that the inquiry will continue to its conclusion.

The board also created a National Security and Export Control Committee of independent directors and said it is searching for a chief compliance officer.

## Markets and Capitol Hill

Nvidia shares closed up 31.5% on Monday, adding nearly $1 trillion in market value, Reuters reported. The gain did not erase all of the losses since Nov. 12. Reuters also reported that Trump owns between $11 million and $55 million in Nvidia stock.

Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer accused the president of putting his own financial interests ahead of national security, according to Reuters. Lawmakers from both parties renewed calls for the Chip Security Act, and Huang has agreed to testify before the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday, Dec. 3, Reuters reported.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Microchip_panel_for_Lunar_Reconnaissance_Orbiter_(LRO).jpg/1280px-Microchip_panel_for_Lunar_Reconnaissance_Orbiter_(LRO).jpg', 'A microchip panel built for NASA''s Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter (file photo, not Nvidia hardware). NASA (public domain) via Wikimedia Commons; editor to confirm the rights statement on the file page', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-24.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-24T11:00:00.000Z', '2026-11-24T11:00:00.000Z');
